<title>USA: Conn. committee snuffs out anti-tobacco proposal.</title>
<headline>Conn. committee snuffs out anti-tobacco proposal.</headline>
<dateline>HARTFORD 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Connecticut legislative committee on Tuesday rejected a proposal to increase the state's tax on cigarettes to six cents to fund anti-tobacco and prevention programs.</p>
<p>The state's Finance Committee defeated the proposal, by Rep. Mary Mushinsky, Democrat, by a vote of 28 to 17, the House Democrats said in a statement.</p>
<p>The initiative would have provided the Department of Mental Health and Addiction Services with the authority to distribute grants to ogranizations offering anti-tobacco education programs for children.</p>
<p>--Hartford newsroom (860) 727-0224</p>
